\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Address map. The slave is selected by the top 5 bits \texttt  {addr[31:27]} (the \textbf  {Base}). Each slave reserves a 128\,MB window (\texttt  {addr[26:0]}) but decodes only the low \textbf  {Offset} bits it needs, \texttt  {addr[7:0]} for every block except the SDRAM snapshot ($^{\ast }$), which decodes \texttt  {addr[12:0]}; the higher window bits are don't care, so each register aliases across them. For S0 the Offset is shown in binary \texttt  {addr[12:0]}: \texttt  {bit\,12} selects the region (\texttt  {0} $=$ status registers, \texttt  {1} $=$ the 512 word spectrum), \texttt  {[10:2]} is the bin index \texttt  {0}\dots  \texttt  {511} and \texttt  {[1:0]} the byte within the word.}}{2}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
